<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ruben Um Nyobe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1913">1913</a>–<a href="/years/1958">1958</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ruben Um Nyobe was a Cameroonian nationalist and secretary-general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-the-peoples-of-cameroon">Union of the Peoples of Cameroon</a>, founded in 1948. He demanded independence and the reunification of French and British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>, and presented the case at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a>. After the party was banned in 1955 he led an armed revolt, and French forces killed him in 1958.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ruben-um-nyobe.jpg" alt="Ruben Um Nyobe" width="300" height="342" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Official Cameroonian photograph · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ruben_Um_Nyobe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
